1
00:04:10,714 --> 00:04:16,714
Heroes don't get any bigger.

2
00:08:21,428 --> 00:08:27,428
Ant-Man is a science fiction, action, adventure film directed by Peyton Reed.

3
00:12:32,142 --> 00:12:38,142
Armed with the astonishing ability to shrink in scale but increase in strength, master thief Scott Lang must embrace his inner-hero and help
his mentor, Doctor Hank Pym, protect the secret behind his spectacular Ant-Man suit from a new generation of towering threats.

4
00:16:42,857 --> 00:16:48,857
Against seemingly insurmountable obstacles, Pym and Lang must
plan and pull off a heist that will save the world.

5
00:20:53,571 --> 00:20:59,571
Scott Lang / Ant-Man, played by Paul Rudd.

6
00:25:04,285 --> 00:25:10,285
Dr. Hank Pym, played by Michael Douglas.

7
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Hope van Dyne, played by Evangeline Lilly.

8
00:33:25,714 --> 00:33:31,714
Darren Cross / Yellowjacket, played by Corey Stoll.

9
00:37:36,428 --> 00:37:42,428
Paxton, played by Bobby Cannavale.

10
00:41:47,142 --> 00:41:53,142
Sam Wilson / Falcon, played by Anthony Mackie.

11
00:45:57,857 --> 00:46:03,857
Ant-Man is a 2015 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics
characters of the same name: Scott Lang and Hank Pym.

12
00:50:08,571 --> 00:50:14,571
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion
Pictures, it is the 12th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
00:54:19,285 --> 00:54:25,285
The film was directed by Peyton Reed from a screenplay by the writing teams
of Edgar Wright & Joe Cornish and Adam McKay & Paul Rudd.

14
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
It stars Rudd as Scott Lang / Ant-Man alongside Evangeline Lilly, Corey Stoll, Bobby Cannavale, Michael Peña, Tip "T.I." Harris,
Anthony Mackie, Wood Harris, Judy Greer, Abby Ryder Fortson, David Dastmalchian, and Michael Douglas as Hank Pym.

15
01:02:40,714 --> 01:02:46,714
In the film, Lang must help defend Pym's Ant-Man shrinking
technology and plot a heist with worldwide ramifications.

16
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
Development of Ant-Man began in April 2006 with the hiring of
Wright to direct and co-write with Cornish.

17
01:11:02,142 --> 01:11:08,142
By April 2011, Wright and Cornish had completed three drafts of the script
and Wright shot test footage for the film in July 2012.

18
01:15:12,857 --> 01:15:18,857
Pre-production began in October 2013 after being put on hold
so that Wright could complete The World's End.

19
01:19:23,571 --> 01:19:29,571
Casting began in December 2013, with the hiring of Rudd to play Lang.

20
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
In May 2014, Wright left the project citing creative differences, though he
still received screenplay and story credits with Cornish.

21
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:51,000
The following month, Reed was brought in to replace Wright, while
McKay was hired to contribute to the script with Rudd.

22
01:31:55,714 --> 01:32:01,714
Filming took place between August and December 2014
in San Francisco and Metro Atlanta.

23
01:36:06,428 --> 01:36:12,428
Ant-Man held its world premiere at the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on June 29, 2015, and
was released in the United States on July 17, as the final film in Phase Two of the MCU.

24
01:40:17,142 --> 01:40:23,142
It grossed more than $519 million worldwide and received positive reviews from critics, who generally welcomed the film's smaller
stakes than other MCU films, as well as its cast (particularly Rudd, Peña, Lilly, and Douglas), humor, and visual effects.

25
01:44:27,857 --> 01:44:33,857
Two sequels have been released: Ant-Man and the Wasp (2018)
and Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania (2023).

26
01:48:38,571 --> 01:48:44,571
The film explores themes of superhero, ant, master
thief, shrinking, based on comic.

27
01:52:49,285 --> 01:52:55,285
The tone is thought_provoking.
